mso-border-left-alt:none;border-right:1.0000pt solid windowtext;mso-border-right-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;
border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;border-bottom:1.0000pt solid windowtext;
mso-border-bottom-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;">
                    <p class=MsoNormal><span style="font-family:仿宋;mso-bidi-font-family:'Times New Roman';font-size:12.0000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><font face="仿宋"><p>Oral mucosal diseases is one of the important components of the clinical courses in the integrated curriculum system of the stomatology major. It involves the contents of multiple disciplines such as oral mucosal diseases, oral histopathology, oral clinical pharmacology, and dermatology and venereology. This course focuses on introducing the etiology, pathogenesis, occurrence, development and prognosis of various common and frequently-occurring oral mucosal diseases and mucosa-skin co-occurring diseases. Clinical manifestations, diagnosis and differential diagnosis, standardized treatment and prevention and treatment principles, clinical manifestations and diagnosis and treatment principles of common systemic diseases in oral mucosa.</p></font></span><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman';mso-fareast-font-family:仿宋;font-size:10.5000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><o:p></o:p></span></p>
                </td>
            </tr>
